00:13:50,069 --> 00:13:52,139
In February 1972,

290
00:13:52,139 --> 00:13:54,379
President Nixon landed in Beijing

291
00:13:54,379 --> 00:13:56,979
He called it the week that changed the world

292
00:14:00,326 --> 00:14:02,836
And it all began with a little plastic ball

293
00:14:02,836 --> 00:14:05,236
weighing less than three grams

294
00:14:12,850 --> 00:14:14,520
In February 1980,

295
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:17,280
the Winter Olympics were held in Lake Placid,

296
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:19,360
in the United States

297
00:14:21,319 --> 00:14:23,709
The Soviet ice hockey team was almost

298
00:14:23,709 --> 00:14:24,549
unbeatable

299
00:14:24,549 --> 00:14:27,429
They had won four Olympic gold medals in a

300
00:14:27,429 --> 00:14:28,549
row

301
00:14:30,424 --> 00:14:32,654
The American team was made up of college

302
00:14:32,654 --> 00:14:33,334
students,

303
00:14:33,334 --> 00:14:35,854
with an average age of around twenty-one

304
00:14:35,854 --> 00:14:37,334
Just before the Games,

305
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:40,094
the Soviets had thrashed them ten goals to

306
00:14:40,094 --> 00:14:41,214
three

307
00:14:43,277 --> 00:14:45,187
On the twenty-second of February,

308
00:14:45,187 --> 00:14:47,627
the two teams met in the medal round

309
00:14:47,627 --> 00:14:50,227
Nobody gave the Americans a chance

310
00:14:52,884 --> 00:14:55,114
Three times the Soviets took the lead,

311
00:14:55,114 --> 00:14:58,343
and every time the Americans fought back to

312
00:14:58,343 --> 00:14:59,463
equalise

313
00:15:01,572 --> 00:15:02,882
In the third period,

314
00:15:02,882 --> 00:15:05,602
captain Mike Eruzione scored

315
00:15:05,602 --> 00:15:07,442
America led four to three

316
00:15:07,442 --> 00:15:10,042
The last ten minutes felt endless

317
00:15:12,659 --> 00:15:14,409
As the clock ran down to zero,

318
00:15:14,409 --> 00:15:16,409
commentator Al Michaels shouted:

319
00:15:16,409 --> 00:15:18,089
do you believe in miracles?

320
00:15:18,089 --> 00:15:19,209
Yes!

321
00:15:22,161 --> 00:15:23,191
Two days later,

322
00:15:23,191 --> 00:15:26,111
the Americans beat Finland to win the gold

323
00:15:26,111 --> 00:15:26,591
medal

324
00:15:26,591 --> 00:15:29,191
That game became known as the Miracle on Ice

325
00:15:37,650 --> 00:15:39,720
By the 1980s,

326
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:42,240
the Soviet economy was exhausted

327
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:44,840
The arms race had simply cost too much

328
00:15:47,665 --> 00:15:48,561
The new leader,

329
00:15:48,561 --> 00:15:49,735
Mikhail Gorbachev,

330
00:15:49,735 --> 00:15:52,135
began to reform and open up the country,

331
00:15:52,135 --> 00:15:54,720
and sat down to negotiate with President

332
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:55,840
Reagan

333
00:15:58,065 --> 00:16:00,695
On the twelfth of June 1987,

334
00:16:00,695 --> 00:16:03,255
standing at the Brandenburg Gate in Berlin,

335
00:16:03,255 --> 00:16:04,095
Reagan said:

336
00:16:04,095 --> 00:16:05,082
Mister Gorbachev,

337
00:16:05,082 --> 00:16:07,162
tear down this wall!

338
00:16:09,611 --> 00:16:11,201
In 1987,

339
00:16:11,201 --> 00:16:13,681
the two sides signed a treaty scrapping an

340
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:16,521
entire class of intermediate-range nuclear

341
00:16:16,521 --> 00:16:17,281
missiles

342
00:16:17,281 --> 00:16:18,681
For the first time,

343
00:16:18,681 --> 00:16:21,081
nuclear arsenals were really cut

344
00:16:23,862 --> 00:16:27,292
On the night of the ninth of November 1989,

345
00:16:27,292 --> 00:16:28,732
the Berlin Wall fell

346
00:16:28,732 --> 00:16:31,572
People from both sides climbed onto the wall,

347
00:16:31,572 --> 00:16:32,612
hugged each other,

348
00:16:32,612 --> 00:16:35,012
and chipped away the concrete

349
00:16:38,803 --> 00:16:39,633
One by one,

350
00:16:39,633 --> 00:16:42,233
the countries of Eastern Europe changed

351
00:16:42,233 --> 00:16:43,593
In 1990,

352
00:16:43,593 --> 00:16:45,353
Germany was reunited

353
00:16:47,914 --> 00:16:50,544
On the evening of the twenty-fifth of December

354
00:16:50,544 --> 00:16:52,084
1991,

355
00:16:52,084 --> 00:16:53,264
Gorbachev resigned

356
00:16:53,264 --> 00:16:55,864
The red flag over the Kremlin was lowered

357
00:16:59,558 --> 00:17:02,148
The Soviet Union broke up into fifteen

358
00:17:02,148 --> 00:17:02,948
countries

359
00:17:02,948 --> 00:17:04,428
The Cold War was over,

360
00:17:04,428 --> 00:17:07,375
with almost no shots fired between the two

361
00:17:07,375 --> 00:17:08,495
superpowers

362
00:17:13,417 --> 00:17:15,607
At its peak in 1986,

363
00:17:15,607 --> 00:17:18,540
the world had around seventy thousand nuclear

364
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:19,194
warheads

365
00:17:19,194 --> 00:17:19,847
Today,

366
00:17:19,847 --> 00:17:22,447
there are still around twelve thousand

367
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,830
For forty-five years,

368
00:17:25,830 --> 00:17:28,350
humanity stood on the brink many times,

369
00:17:28,350 --> 00:17:30,950
and was lucky enough to step back

370
00:17:32,674 --> 00:17:34,504
Some heroes never needed a gun:

371
00:17:34,504 --> 00:17:36,184
a pilot dropping candy,

372
00:17:36,184 --> 00:17:37,664
a table tennis player,

373
00:17:37,664 --> 00:17:40,264
the people who dared to cross a wall

374
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:44,190
Which story surprised you the most?

375
00:17:44,190 --> 00:17:46,790
Let me know in the comments
